From 65c070a26fb86085e2de5690224db0cf9902b5ce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kernel-wasm <kernel-wasm@localhost>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 08:27:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wasm: parking and snapshots on SMP

KW_PARK no longer depends on !SMP. kwparkd, bound to CPU 0, parks last
and starts a rendezvous: every other CPU that reaches idle with nothing
pending checks in and blocks with interrupts off, and CPU 0 claims them,
checks that every task is parked and off its CPU, and takes the snapshot
after its irqentry_exit(), so that every idle task is saved in the same
state. A CPU that is not claimed yet leaves on an IPI or its timer; the
window for a missing CPU grows with each retry up to the cycle's
deadline.

kw_unpark() marks a task under task_call_func(): one that is off its CPU
restarts on a fresh stack, one still on its old stack carries on there.
A resumed task keeps its single migrate_disable() hold, so parked tasks
stay on their CPU.

A restored snapshot enters kw_resume on CPU 0, which resets the per-CPU
state and starts the other CPUs again through wasm_cpu_start(); they
enter kw_secondary_resume. Each CPU leaves the saved idle state as its
old stack would have (ct_cpuidle_exit(), tick_nohz_idle_exit()) and
starts a new idle loop. kwparkd waits for every CPU before it steps the
clock, runs the restore notifiers and resumes the tasks. A parked task
woken before that starts on a fresh stack and waits there.
---
