+ * checks the tasks; a held CPU that gets an IPI or whose timer expires
+ * before it is claimed leaves (the sender may wait for it) and checks in
+ * again. When the claims find something to do first (a task still on its
+ * way to sleep, an interrupt for CPU 0), CPU 0 gives the claimed CPUs back
